    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining current JPM positions rather than adding or exiting. The technical picture is bullish (price $184.66 above 10 EMA $181.76, 50 SMA $180.59, and 200 SMA $154.91; MACD just crossed positive; RSI 56.95 with room before overbought), and fundamentals available are fortress-grade ($3.88T assets, $327.9B equity, $25.6B returned to shareholders). However, the recovery has occurred on weak relative volume (0.60, 40% below average), the MACD crossover is a single-day event, and price sits just 1-2% below an untested resistance zone at $186.5-188.9. Critically, Q1 2024 earnings details, credit quality metrics, and capital ratios are unavailable as of April 26, 2024, making a high-conviction BUY unjustified. The trend and fundamentals are too strong for a Sell, but the unconfirmed breakout, weak volume, and data gaps argue for patience. The cleanest entries are a confirmed breakout above $188.90 on strong volume or a pullback to the $180-182 support confluence.\n\n**Entry Price**: 184.66\n\n**Stop Loss**: 178.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position size at or below normal given elevated ATR of $3.27; do not add new exposure at $184.66\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
